Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.22,0:00:06.17,Default,Sylvia,0,0,0,,Nark?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.06,0:00:08.23,Default,Sylvia,0,0,0,,No, it's not!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.23,0:00:09.59,Default,Kav,0,0,0,,Let's bring it down!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.99,0:00:17.24,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I finally managed to catch it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.59,0:00:20.20,Default,Sylvia,0,0,0,,What is that thing?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.20,0:00:23.98,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oscar brought it back from a ruins expedition.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.98,0:00:29.43,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,He told me it was a stone egg, \Nbut it must have hatched at some point.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.66,0:00:34.76,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Great work reformulating \Na suitable spell so quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.41,0:00:39.31,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Or perhaps it's only natural \Nfor our new chief mage...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.58,0:00:40.69,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Valt.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.69,0:00:42.80,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I'm honored, Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.16,0:02:18.99,Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)}~ Once upon a Time with You ~
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.17,0:02:22.21,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}How many cycles have I lived now?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.21,0:02:23.99,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've never tried counting.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.45,0:02:29.42,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}However, this is the first time \NI've joined the Farsas royal court.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.42,0:02:30.72,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I swear!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.72,0:02:32.38,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Bringing back such a suspicious item!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.83,0:02:36.21,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Spirit sorcerer ruins \Nare full of dangerous things!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.21,0:02:37.59,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Okay, I get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.59,0:02:40.26,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I can tell you don't from that reply!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.78,0:02:43.80,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,It was likely used for patrolling.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.26,0:02:45.42,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.42,0:02:49.54,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,However, it contains \Nan unfamiliar spell composition.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.54,0:02:51.52,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll set about analyzing it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.52,0:02:52.34,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.01,0:02:56.19,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,So, how did the towns to the east look?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.49,0:03:00.15,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,You mean the increase in sudden deaths \Nand suicides of unknown cause?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.46,0:03:03.15,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Quite frankly, \Nthe investigation's not going well.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.15,0:03:08.26,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Even those who escape death end up \Nlosing their sanity or falling into a coma.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.26,0:03:09.12,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.42,0:03:14.60,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Many of the casualties are mages, \Nwith their magic going haywire,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.60,0:03:18.78,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,but the postmortems don't tell us much \Nabout their condition.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.18,0:03:20.28,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.28,0:03:24.05,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,The barrier around the castle city \Ndoesn't allow demons to pass, does it?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.05,0:03:25.21,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That's correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.21,0:03:29.27,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Though it won't do much \Nagainst the highest-ranking ones.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.27,0:03:33.31,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Then can you set up the same barrier \Naround the towns and villages to the east?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.31,0:03:36.48,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Yes, but not all at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.80,0:03:38.65,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Whatever you can manage is fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.14,0:03:41.70,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Five days before the first unnatural death...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.02,0:03:45.70,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,At Minnedart Fortress, \Nwhich guards the eastern border,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.70,0:03:48.11,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,a mage fell from a rampart to his death.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.03,0:03:51.96,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,If we assume it was the same cause of death...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.25,0:03:57.72,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,It'd mean whatever's causing the deaths \Nis approaching us from the east.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.33,0:04:07.18,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}What I've learned from living countless lives
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.18,0:04:11.60,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}is the fact that things you have \Nno knowledge of occur all the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.12,0:04:16.24,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}I knew nothing of the king bringing back \Na mysterious egg from the ruins,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.24,0:04:19.44,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}nor of the outbreak \Nof suspicious deaths within Farsas.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.86,0:04:22.49,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}Last month, there was an expedition \Nfrom Minnedart Fortress
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.49,0:04:25.58,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}to subdue the Ito, an equestrian tribe.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.58,0:04:27.42,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}That was also new to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.77,0:04:32.28,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,It'd be best to write it \Nall down in the records...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.05,0:04:35.32,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,The records, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.90,0:04:39.22,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Could this all be meaningless?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.84,0:04:43.80,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,Valt. The food's ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.03,0:04:46.26,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I'll be right there.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.23,0:04:51.13,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,Anything interesting \Nhappen lately in the castle?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.13,0:04:54.19,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I go there to do work, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.19,0:04:56.61,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I saw a stone bird flying around the palace.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.61,0:04:57.54,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,Made of stone?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.54,0:04:59.07,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,How does it fly?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.07,0:05:03.36,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,In the Dark Age, people did research \Non similar magical creatures.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.36,0:05:07.20,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,The queen is going to analyze it, \Nso I'll ask her to show me the spell diagram.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.97,0:05:11.16,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,You sound so enthusiastic \Nwhenever you talk about magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.44,0:05:14.33,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,I wish I'd been born with magic, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.33,0:05:17.04,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I'm lending you my magic, aren't I?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.04,0:05:18.99,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,That's nothing but a mark.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.99,0:05:21.24,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,It's not like I can use magic with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.96,0:05:29.09,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,On that note, strange deaths have been \Ncropping up recently east of here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.61,0:05:32.86,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,His Majesty thinks \Nit might be the work of demons.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.86,0:05:34.39,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Make sure you keep an eye out.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.00,0:05:36.20,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.20,0:05:39.88,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,But it's not like I ever leave the castle city.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.88,0:05:41.56,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,I have no reason to.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.56,0:05:42.92,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Just making sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.62,0:05:55.96,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Which one of us do you need?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.96,0:05:57.21,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Her Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.21,0:05:59.60,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,There's a merchant caravan \Nwith a demonic beast in tow,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.60,0:06:01.75,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,asking for an inspection \Nto enter the castle city.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.03,0:06:05.82,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,If you would grant me the authority, \NI can handle it for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.82,0:06:07.72,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Ask Valt to deal with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.72,0:06:10.92,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,With how weary you are, \Nit'll be a while until you're fit to be seen.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.90,0:06:13.72,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Please do, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.05,0:06:15.36,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,As you wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.11,0:06:19.74,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Are those the same birds?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.22,0:06:22.83,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,They're smaller now.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.83,0:06:24.37,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Fascinating, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.37,0:06:26.80,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I made copies of them following my analysis.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.34,0:06:29.92,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It seems they were created to patrol after all,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.92,0:06:32.83,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,but they're equipped with \Na spraying mechanism, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.61,0:06:34.84,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Spraying?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.09,0:06:38.89,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It looks like it wants to come along.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.73,0:06:44.86,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,Valt?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.72,0:06:47.95,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Miralys.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.95,0:06:49.31,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,What's with the flowers?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.31,0:06:50.80,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,They're for decoration back home.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.12,0:06:53.30,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Don't you think that's an awful lot?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.30,0:06:58.27,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,At the shop I always go to, they had \Na customer back out of an order.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.27,0:07:01.22,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,I bought all the flowers \Nto help their predicament.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.22,0:07:03.00,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Miralys, you're a kind girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.09,0:07:06.30,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,That's not true at all...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.36,0:07:11.53,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,Say, what's that on your shoulder?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.87,0:07:15.49,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,This is a magical creature made by Her Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.74,0:07:18.58,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,Can I pet it later?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.96,0:07:20.14,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Go right ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.00,0:07:25.09,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,Huh? What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.09,0:07:26.93,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I'm not sure, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.93,0:07:27.72,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I think...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.68,0:07:41.82,Default-Top,Valt,0,0,0,,That's Tris and...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.15,0:07:44.15,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,500)\pos(203,290)}Savas    {\fs14}Prince of Yarda
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.82,0:07:43.95,Default-Top,Valt,0,0,0,,the Yarda prince, Savas?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.04,0:07:46.35,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Why are they here?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.11,0:07:48.22,Default,Savas,0,0,0,,Go on.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.61,0:07:53.79,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Miralys!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.18,0:08:06.08,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Miralys...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.15,0:08:15.82,Default,Savas,0,0,0,,Feast your eyes on this, Leonora!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.82,0:08:18.82,Default,Savas,0,0,0,,This spells the end for that witch!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.14,0:08:30.28,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}I thought I'd understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.70,0:08:35.21,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}The fact that things I have \Nno knowledge of occur all the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.43,0:08:38.90,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}She will never open her eyes again.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.31,0:08:43.21,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's no trace left of her soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.15,0:08:46.80,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}The world waits for its chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.69,0:08:51.71,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}Which is why, at times, \Nit can catch up to her like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.38,0:08:57.72,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}As though to say, "This is as far as you go."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.68,0:09:12.61,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,That which robs mages of their sanity, \Nforces their magic to go haywire,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.61,0:09:15.35,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,and devastates their spirits and lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.77,0:09:22.23,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Irityrdia, the sole god of Tayiri, \Nwas what had been sealed inside Tris.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.74,0:09:24.20,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You know of it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.78,0:09:29.06,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Irityrdia, freed last month in \Nthe aftermath of the fight against the Ito,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.06,0:09:32.34,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,had been slowly making its way \Nwhile causing death around it,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.34,0:09:33.76,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,until it was captured in its path.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.35,0:09:38.07,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Savas must have been \Nafter Tinasha from the very start.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.81,0:09:43.64,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,An act of vengeance for killing Leonora, \Nthe witch he had worshiped?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.98,0:09:49.40,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,The stone birds were spraying \Na psychological safeguard against Irityrdia.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.95,0:09:52.40,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It's thanks to them that you're still sane
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.40,0:09:55.61,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,after you came in close contact \Nwith that thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.23,0:09:58.83,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Three hundred dead in three days' time.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.65,0:10:02.82,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,To contain Irityrdia, \Nwhich had been growing stronger,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.82,0:10:07.07,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,our only choice was to destroy it \Nwith Akashia while Tinasha was its vessel.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.29,0:10:11.60,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,She was the one who was \Nthe most careless with her own life.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.43,0:10:17.26,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,So in exchange, I wanted to treat it \Nwith more care than anyone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.33,0:10:22.23,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I'm certain Queen Tinasha \Nunderstood that the best.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.21,0:10:29.00,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,The blame lies with me \Nfor being unable to prevent this.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.71,0:10:32.65,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'm sorry for making you go through this.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.91,0:10:36.11,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Here's to your health and prosperity.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.77,0:10:40.56,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Until we meet in another time, \Nin another manner.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.09,0:10:43.27,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Yeah. You too.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.90,0:10:57.93,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,If you could turn back time \Nand redo everything,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.33,0:11:00.26,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,what do you think you'd do?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.48,0:11:05.93,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'm afraid I can't say.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.88,0:11:08.89,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,But I do know...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.35,0:11:14.44,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That if it was for my own sake, \NI wouldn't be able to go through with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.02,0:11:24.70,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,The you here is a different you from before.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.23,0:11:27.54,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,That's a thought I couldn't help but entertain.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.01,0:11:30.30,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,But you are you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.30,0:11:32.48,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,The world will not diverge.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.48,0:11:37.50,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Throughout every cycle, \Nyour soul is unique to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.35,0:11:48.67,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Which is why I'm going to go see you again...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.76,0:11:51.91,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Miralys.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.71,0:11:57.79,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,Valt?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.98,0:12:06.41,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,You were sleeping out here?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.45,0:12:08.82,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Good morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.82,0:12:11.62,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,You must be tired, dozing off like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.10,0:12:13.62,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I'm fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.62,0:12:16.25,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I was just dreaming about the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.23,0:12:22.67,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}Events from the distant past, \Nwhich no longer exist at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.13,0:12:27.70,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}Precious memories that remain nowhere else.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.40,0:12:35.34,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What's up?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.34,0:12:37.07,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Huh? Oscar?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.85,0:12:40.37,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I got lost in thought concentrating.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.37,0:12:41.65,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,My apologies.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.93,0:12:43.81,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What were you thinking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.81,0:12:45.86,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Your brows were furrowed.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.16,0:12:47.76,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,This and that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.08,0:12:52.98,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oscar, do you know the tale of \Nthe Mirror of Oblivion?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.63,0:12:58.04,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Yeah, I think it's about a mirror \Nthat takes all your sadness away.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.04,0:13:01.05,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,500)}Mirror of Oblivion
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.33,0:13:01.80,Default-Top,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's an old fairy tale \Ndating back to the early Dark Age.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.80,0:13:05.81,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,But in some regions, it takes away \Nyour memories instead of sadness,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.81,0:13:08.38,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,or makes you fall asleep \Nafter absorbing your spirit.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.38,0:13:10.29,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It changes a little each time.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.29,0:13:12.27,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Huh, interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.27,0:13:17.80,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,And tracing all the accounts, the last place \Nthe mirror is said to have been seen is...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.80,0:13:19.26,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Magdalsia, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.16,0:13:25.20,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You think that fairy tale has something \Nto do with the witch in Magdalsia?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.52,0:13:28.66,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,If all the Witch of the Forbidden Forest \Nwanted was to control the nation,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.66,0:13:33.16,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,it'd be easier to control the king's mind \Ninstead of putting him into a coma.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.16,0:13:37.84,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You mean the witch appeared \N{\i1}because{\i0} the king fell ill?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.84,0:13:39.68,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Or so I suspect.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.68,0:13:44.38,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What caused the mysterious coma \Nand summoned the witch?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.08,0:13:50.14,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.08,0:13:57.27,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I think I'll go see what's \Nhappening in Magdalsia after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.27,0:13:58.23,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.69,0:14:00.80,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Not a chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.80,0:14:02.80,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,There's no need for you to meddle.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.80,0:14:06.65,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm the only human who can fight \Nthe Witch of the Forbidden Forest.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.96,0:14:09.28,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Even so...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.28,0:14:11.86,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,She wields the royal authority of Magdalsia.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.12,0:14:16.12,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,With your standing, you could \Nvery well end up causing a war.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.46,0:14:18.60,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You'll send us back to the Dark Age.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.60,0:14:20.75,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm sure things will work themselves out.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.75,0:14:21.91,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tinasha!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.34,0:14:28.02,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You have no right to stop me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.15,0:14:33.44,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Didn't you travel \Nfour hundred years to be with me?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.77,0:14:39.19,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The two of us would be enemies \Nif not for the times we live in.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.74,0:14:50.49,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I don't know what goes on in your head.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.59,0:14:56.86,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,There were quite a few heads \Nof our family before me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.33,0:15:01.37,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,These are the records of \Nthe countless fragments of their lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.37,0:15:04.21,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,Have you ever written these, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.21,0:15:05.59,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,A number of times.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.97,0:15:10.44,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,The events that came to pass, \Nwhat changed between different cycles...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.44,0:15:12.72,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,If there's anything I want \Nto tell those who succeed me,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.72,0:15:14.19,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,writing this is the only way.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.62,0:15:18.79,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,There's no need to look so grim.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.79,0:15:22.36,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,The people who wrote this down \Ndid so of their own volition.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.36,0:15:26.23,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,There are records of the Witch \Nof the Azure Moon in here, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.56,0:15:27.63,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Yes, there are.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.63,0:15:31.88,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,That said, she very rarely \Ncame down from her tower.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.88,0:15:35.45,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I'd say I know more than what's \Nbeen documented here.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.86,0:15:38.51,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Since I know her from when she was queen...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.91,0:15:40.37,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,Wh-What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.08,0:15:42.26,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Don't tell me...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.26,0:15:44.83,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,She ignored Magdalsia and came here instead?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.47,0:15:50.95,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Miralys, this way!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.23,0:15:56.05,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,If you think I'd fail to act, \Nyou're sorely mistaken.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.05,0:15:57.29,Default,Miralys,0,0,0,,Valt?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.29,0:15:58.01,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,It's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.01,0:15:59.76,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I can't have these remain.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.39,0:16:04.35,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is this the side of her \NI don't know, as a Dark Age ruler?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.82,0:16:10.20,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Not bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.20,0:16:12.56,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,He's put up a pretty strong barrier.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.56,0:16:14.28,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Time to penetrate it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.84,0:16:27.94,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,A girl?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.77,0:16:33.05,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Writings?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.05,0:16:34.09,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Sorry, Lady Tinasha.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.38,0:16:36.80,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,They got away.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.83,0:16:39.26,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Lady Tinasha?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.45,0:16:56.71,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,He ticks me off.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.71,0:16:59.53,Default,Als,0,0,0,,Looks like Queen Tinasha's not here yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.87,0:17:02.07,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,She seems pretty busy lately.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.70,0:17:05.43,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,At least she gave up \Non taking action all by herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.81,0:17:10.71,Default,Als,0,0,0,,Here she is.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.35,0:17:18.96,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Didn't bother to dress up, I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.96,0:17:20.60,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Not to mention you're late.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.60,0:17:22.21,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I barely made it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.21,0:17:24.56,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I haven't eaten since this morning, either...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.91,0:17:26.71,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Today hasn't been a good day.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.68,0:17:29.08,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Here, something sugary.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.08,0:17:31.10,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Starting off with dessert?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.28,0:17:38.19,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Why'd you call me over?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.66,0:17:40.62,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Something troubling has come to light.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.42,0:17:42.83,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Let's get right to the point.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.21,0:17:46.04,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Do you have memories of time repeating?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.35,0:17:48.25,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Oh, is that all?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.25,0:17:50.03,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Nope, no memories.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.03,0:17:52.49,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Since those orbs are outsiders' artifacts.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.49,0:17:53.96,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Outsiders' artifacts?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.96,0:17:56.42,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,What? Never heard of them?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.88,0:18:03.66,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,In simple terms, it refers to all artifacts \Nwith powers that defy the laws of magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.66,0:18:06.14,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,I'm susceptible to their effects, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.14,0:18:07.35,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Are you really?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.74,0:18:10.18,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You behave strangely at times.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.18,0:18:13.60,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Like you know what the future holds, \Nor you've experienced it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.60,0:18:15.57,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,I really don't know! Lay off it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.57,0:18:20.28,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Travis, I saw records of a history \Nthat no longer exists.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.64,0:18:24.65,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Before history changed, Cezar thrived \Nas a wealthy Great Nation,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.65,0:18:27.25,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,and it never invaded Farsas.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.52,0:18:29.72,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,You saw all that?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.28,0:18:34.49,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Aurelia, go run off and play.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.49,0:18:35.56,Default,Aurelia,0,0,0,,What? I can't...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.56,0:18:36.59,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Off you go.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.59,0:18:38.63,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Make sure you don't follow strangers.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.31,0:18:50.23,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Let me begin by saying that \NI really don't have any memories.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.23,0:18:53.40,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,However, I've come across records as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.19,0:18:56.47,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,A family known as the Time-Readers:
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.94,0:19:00.09,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,they retain their memories \Nthrough repeated histories,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.09,0:19:03.40,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,and these extensive memories \Nare written down and passed on.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.04,0:19:05.46,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,The current family head is...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.46,0:19:06.33,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Valt.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.29,0:19:09.57,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Tell us more about them.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.57,0:19:10.75,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Why should I?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.00,0:19:13.21,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Valt is after Eleterria!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.50,0:19:14.67,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.96,0:19:18.68,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Why are they called \N"outsiders' artifacts," anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.68,0:19:20.82,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I've never even heard the term before.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.82,0:19:23.64,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,That's because their \Nvery existence is problematic.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.64,0:19:26.53,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Not exactly the kind of thing \Nyou can blabber on about.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.53,0:19:29.53,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,We're talking about items introduced \Nfrom outside our world.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.37,0:19:33.10,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,So there really does exist something out there?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.10,0:19:36.82,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Well, whether you believe it \Nor not is up to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.14,0:19:41.56,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Even if there {\i1}are{\i0} beings that get their kicks \Nfrom watching you humans from outside,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.56,0:19:43.28,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,what's it matter, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.28,0:19:50.25,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Like how the characters in a book aren't \Naware of the world outside the book?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.56,0:19:55.06,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,It's futile to even try and \Nunderstand what they're thinking.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.06,0:19:58.18,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,I met one of them a long time ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.18,0:20:00.47,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,A completely unfathomable woman.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.47,0:20:02.48,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You {\i1}met{\i0} one of them?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.48,0:20:03.17,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That's not fair!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.17,0:20:05.87,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's like you were given all the answers!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.97,0:20:05.87,Default-Top,Travis,0,0,0,,Quiet!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.87,0:20:07.81,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,It's your fault for being ignorant.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.81,0:20:11.28,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Besides, that woman was an outsider, \Nbut also not really.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.69,0:20:16.01,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Choosing to align herself with humans, \Nshe lived and died among them.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.01,0:20:18.62,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Long before you were ever born.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.38,0:20:21.22,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,She was the only one of her kind,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.22,0:20:23.95,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,and she's got nothing to do \Nwith the outsiders' artifacts.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.95,0:20:25.20,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Are you talking about...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.20,0:20:26.16,Default,Magistrate,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.16,0:20:27.87,Default,Magistrate,0,0,0,,I have an urgent message!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.87,0:20:31.81,Default,Magistrate,0,0,0,,Magdalsian soldiers have just crossed \Nthe border and begun their invasion!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.81,0:20:33.39,Default,Magistrate,0,0,0,,Their army is about thirty thousand men!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.39,0:20:36.58,Default,Magistrate,0,0,0,,In half an hour, they'll make contact \Nwith a Tuldarr village to the south!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.58,0:20:37.73,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What'd you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.73,0:20:40.05,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That was sooner than I'd expected.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.05,0:20:41.50,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.50,0:20:43.26,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Please tell the troops to mobilize.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.26,0:20:44.96,Default,Magistrate,0,0,0,,Right away!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.96,0:20:47.22,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I must leave now to attend to this matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.56,0:20:49.52,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Thank you for your time, Travis.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.18,0:20:56.10,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Magdalsia has chosen war, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.78,0:20:59.39,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,She's finally back to her old self.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.39,0:21:01.99,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,I was wondering when she'd grow a spine again.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.98,0:21:04.77,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Don't give me that look.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.77,0:21:07.20,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,She's always been like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.72,0:21:11.54,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Following up on earlier...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.54,0:21:13.55,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Don't hand over Eleterria.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.55,0:21:15.17,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,I'd rather not do everything over.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.17,0:21:17.50,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Don't use them or have them stolen.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.28,0:21:23.31,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,I don't plan on giving up Aurelia, \Nor the rest of this history.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.50,0:21:27.95,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Change of plans.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.95,0:21:29.13,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'm going back to Farsas.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.93,0:21:39.76,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,{\i1}Tinasha viewed herself \Nas foreign to this era all along.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.44,0:21:44.90,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Could it be that she never \Nintended to become my queen?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.57,0:21:51.50,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Who goes there?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.26,0:21:57.10,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Forgive the intrusion, \Nbut I was hoping we could talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.54,0:21:58.89,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Valt...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.47,0:23:40.02,Next Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)}~ At Memory's End ~
